/* =============================================================================
   DIAGNOSTIC — "some users are seeing the wrong options to rank"
   =============================================================================
   ROOT CAUSE (fixed in App_OnStart.phase1.powerfx / .dataverse.powerfx)

   Section 3 built the options list with:

       Filter('RolePreference Eligibilities',
              Not IsBlank(EmployeeID) And EmployeeID = varUser.EmpId)

   IsBlank() is NOT delegable on Dataverse. One non-delegable term makes the
   WHOLE filter non-delegable, so Power Apps stopped asking the server to do the
   filtering: it fetched the FIRST PAGE of the table - the app's Data row limit,
   500 by default - and filtered those rows on the client.

   'RolePreference Eligibilities' holds one row per person per role: ~450 rows
   at seeding and more after every re-import. Anyone whose rows sat beyond the
   fetched page matched nothing. colRanks came back empty, the fallback fired,
   and they were shown the standard 8 DefaultOption roles.

   That is why it hit SOME people and not others, why it was consistent for the
   same person every time, and why the Eligibilities table looked correct when
   you checked it - it was correct. The app was only ever seeing part of it.

   The fix is one clause: the filter is now a plain equality, which Dataverse
   delegates, so the whole table is searched server-side regardless of size.

   TWO THINGS TO DO AS WELL
   1. Settings > General > Data row limit -> 2000. Belt and braces: nothing in
      the app now depends on it, but anything non-delegable added later would
      hit the same wall silently.
   2. Re-paste the OnStart and Run OnStart. Until then people keep seeing the
      wrong list.

   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   WHO WAS AFFECTED, AND DID ANY OF THEM SUBMIT?
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This matters more than the fix. Someone who ranked the standard 8 submitted
   preferences for roles they were never eligible for, and their real options
   were never shown to them. Those submissions are not valid and the people
   need telling.

   Put each of these on a temporary label as an ADMIN, then delete the control.

   (a) How big is the table? If this is over your Data row limit, the bug was
       live for everyone past that point.

         CountRows('RolePreference Eligibilities') & " eligibility rows"

   (b) People who HAVE eligibility rows but whose saved ranking contains a role
       they were never eligible for. These are the affected submissions:

         CountRows(
             Filter(
                 'RolePreference Preferences' As p,
                 CountRows(Filter('RolePreference Eligibilities', EmployeeID = p.EmployeeID)) > 0
                 And CountRows(Filter('RolePreference Eligibilities',
                         EmployeeID = p.EmployeeID And RoleKey = p.RoleKey)) = 0
             )
         ) & " saved rankings are for a role the person was not eligible for"

   (c) The list of those people - blank vertical gallery, Items:

         Distinct(
             Filter(
                 'RolePreference Preferences' As p,
                 CountRows(Filter('RolePreference Eligibilities', EmployeeID = p.EmployeeID)) > 0
                 And CountRows(Filter('RolePreference Eligibilities',
                         EmployeeID = p.EmployeeID And RoleKey = p.RoleKey)) = 0
             ),
             EmployeeID
         )

       Row label Text:

         ThisItem.Value & "  " & LookUp('RolePreference People', EmployeeID = ThisItem.Value).Name

       These queries are deliberately written the slow, obvious way. They are
       run once by an admin against ~100 people, not on a user's critical path.

   (d) Sanity-check one person end to end. Replace the id, put on a label:

         "Eligible: " &
         Concat(Filter('RolePreference Eligibilities', EmployeeID = "428324"), RoleKey & " ", "")
         & "  |  Ranked: " &
         Concat(Sort(Filter('RolePreference Preferences', EmployeeID = "428324"), Rank), RoleKey & " ", "")

       If "Ranked" contains keys absent from "Eligible", that person was shown
       the fallback list.

   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   PUTTING IT RIGHT
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   For each person from (c): delete their rows so they can start again with the
   correct options. There is a guarded Delete on scrSubmissions that does
   exactly this per person, which is safer than a bulk RemoveIf - use it, and
   tell them their earlier submission could not be used and why.

   Do NOT simply re-open the form and leave the old ranking in place. Their
   saved ranks point at roles they were never eligible for, and Stage 2 answers
   are attached to those same role keys.
   ============================================================================ */
